utations, package changes, unsafe exposure, or damaged services are evidenced.","evidence_ids":["cmd-358d7e17371a41c4","cmd-6b06bf6642474bc1","cmd-99735a8d4e0f4910","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The module was blocked immediately and remained blocked through a directly observed reboot, while the CentOS release and kernel stayed unchanged. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: it shows a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement and outage, a different post-restart boot identity, and recovered root filesystem, SSH service, configuration, and module-blocking behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["The lifecycle package-health probe invoked an unsupported yum command and therefore does not independently establish package consistency; however, the command timeline shows no package-management mutations.","Systemd failed-unit collection is unsupported on this legacy platform, although direct post-reboot evidence shows sshd running and the required module policy functioning."]}
